{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/856860-allies-and-contacts-ideas","id":856860,"title":"Allies and Contacts ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-31T19:22:28-07:00","id":856860,"title":"Allies and Contacts ideas","content":"We all know the basic Allies and Contacts: City Hall, Police, Crime Organization, etc. But I need to stat up about 40 NPCs, and I'm looking for new ideas, and you guys are awesome for this kind of stuff. And it's not just for me, I think this could useful for others as well.<br /> <br /> So, I'm using my 1 dot in &quot;Contacts (Onyx Path Forum)&quot;... <br /> <br /> What are some other interesting Allies or Contacts that you've used, or seen used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:58:12-07:00","id":856882,"title":"","content":"Roland Deeker the cab/limo dispatcher, need a ride any time of night call the deekman. Probably strung out on something but he can get you a ride anywhere.<br /> <br /> Lou &quot;Scarface&quot; strassmore, door man at the hottest night club in town. For a fee he's willing to look the other way if your packing or if you need a little heat yourself.<br /> <br /> Sid &quot;no nose&quot; Halsey, runs the over night pawn window, don't ask about what happened to his nose and he can make most things disappear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T20:23:33-07:00","id":856894,"title":"","content":"Groups: Masonic Lodge, amateur UFO hunters, Kemetic neopagans, Civil War reenactors, HEMA troupe, elementary school PTA, Vietnam veterans breakfast club, 1950s car collectors, Natural History Museum volunteers, internet harassment group with an obnoxious hashtag, wealthy fursuiters.<br /> <br /> Specific individuals: tattoo shop owner, &quot;professional&quot; paranormal debunker, kosher butcher, guy who makes and repairs antique firearms, intern at a major newspaper, mortician.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T22:55:51-07:00","id":856966,"title":"","content":"A cat burglar had contacts in the in the Security industry (safes, sensors, alarms, etc.). She presented herself at a convention as an independent contractor, then got insider connections she could use to both practice on new vaults and other systems being released and call up to find out what specific systems and equipment a particular person or company bought to prepare for jobs.<br /> <br /> That said, uh, why are you actually filing out complete character sheets for 40 people? I can't ever imagine doing that. Even if you want attributes and skills (which I still would never do), why do you need to do specific Contacts and Allies? When is that ever going to come up? Do you, like, play out scenes with NPCs rolling to connect with their Contacts? I don't understand when this would be helpful or worth the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2698-the-storyteller","name":"The Storyteller","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T23:19:47-07:00","id":856972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/856860-allies-and-contacts-ideas?p=856966#post856966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cat burglar had contacts in the in the Security industry (safes, sensors, alarms, etc.). She presented herself at a convention as an independent contractor, then got insider connections she could use to both practice on new vaults and other systems being released and call up to find out what specific systems and equipment a particular person or company bought to prepare for jobs.<br /> <br /> That said, uh, why are you actually filing out complete character sheets for 40 people? I can't ever imagine doing that. Even if you want attributes and skills (which I still would never do), why do you need to do specific Contacts and Allies? When is that ever going to come up? Do you, like, play out scenes with NPCs rolling to connect with their Contacts? I don't understand when this would be helpful or worth the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>My go-to for NPCs is stolen from the Storytelling Adventure System; rather than say &quot;oh, this ninja has these Attributes and these Skills,&quot; just come up with the most likely dice pools, like Throw Shuriken (5 dice) or Vanish Into Shadows (7 dice).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T00:08:50-07:00","id":856991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Storyteller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/856860-allies-and-contacts-ideas?p=856966#post856966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> That said, uh, why are you actually filing out complete character sheets for 40 people? I can't ever imagine doing that. Even if you want attributes and skills (which I still would never do), why do you need to do specific Contacts and Allies? When is that ever going to come up? Do you, like, play out scenes with NPCs rolling to connect with their Contacts? I don't understand when this would be helpful or worth the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am filling out complete character sheets. Because PC's can go to NPCs for favors, and I'd like to know who can offer what. Or the NPCs can use those same merits against the PCs if they piss them off. Allies can be used to counter opponents from using their contacts, etc. I also like knowing who can do what. I suppose I could just decide on the spot, but in the case the NPC become antagonistic, I don't want to cheese it. Yes, it's a lot of work, but considering the amount of details I'm putting into the political hierarchy, domains and locations, I have no problem doing the same for it's notable inhabitants.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the replies, everyone... hoping for even more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":231,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","user":"Blitzburger","date":". 04-01-2016, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:38:03-07:00","id":857074,"title":"","content":"This might seem overly regiment, but I would adhere to some sort of system.<br /> <br /> For example,<br /> <br /> Figure out the different 'spheres' of influence as you alluded to in your first post, then create a list of allies for each sphere like: five '1 dot' Allies, six '2 dot' allies, five '3 dot' allies, four '4 dot' allies, and three '5 dot' allies. Also, I would try to get player input, too - like, give them some free dots in Allies and Contacts at character creation, let them have a hand in creating the setting - like, 2 free dots in Allies, 1 free dot in Contacts. That way they're automatically inclined to build three NPCs that give them a link into the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T05:51:05-07:00","id":857076,"title":"","content":"Local detective agency; mortal fight club whose members are unwittingly transforming into something between hunter and slasher; lawyer aware of the world beyond the night and who offers help to those who might pay for it; MD who will save anyone, even if they are not human; black market doctor; journalist from local SUPERNATURAL MAGAZINE; pizza delivery girl whose fate seems to be &quot;always take it to weird people and see weird shit&quot;; cult; FBI agent; Assasin who doesn't take money, just body parts from the victims (and only from victims she has a contract on, too); neighborhood union; teacher in school; hypercurious kids from school; union of homeless people; mortician; retired university professor with a lot of dots in academics and occult; master thief; clean-up specialist who takes less money for extra grotesque crimes as long as they can take their time and paint it; pastor or priest from church; nun taking care of abandoned children; a man believing himself to be a host of ten thousand feathers, whose random insights provide to be useful in bizzare ways; ruthless pawnbroker who will sell and buy anything if it has price, and cares about supernatural...if it makes profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T08:00:39-07:00","id":857128,"title":"","content":"I would advise you to do something like this - when your character need for someone, take a Character, a quirk and a motivation. <br /> If you wish you may also take a special thing or two. <br /> <br /> Otherwhise, steal all the possible characters from fiction (i would advise breaking bad, better call soul.)<br /> <br /> Character: pusher with a painful past and stars in his eyes; overhelpful and gaudy priest; shady psychiatrist that sells medicines as drugs; extreme sport enthusiast CEO; not so competent lawyer that uses more their charisma than their knowledge of law; gruff mathemathician with a passion for theology; first time outlaw with a million dollar; ambitious cleaning service personnel; high school student with all his future already planned by themself and a ground breaking invention.<br /> <br /> <br /> Quirk: smokes horrible honey scented cigars; stutters - but everyone fears them nonetheless; has everytime some food with them; use a horrible southern accent in order to appear more affable; speaks too much, even when they should not; likes to meet in unusual places and surprise the others; devastating skin condition; is able to tell when anyone lies; gets agitated for nothing; hands bleached by chemicals, shifty eyes; keeps the conversation straight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Motivation: have a lot of money to change career; repay someone else of a debt; have the love or respect of someone else; have a petty revenge; share their vision; have a specific object they could not obtain otherwise (it is illegal, lost or unique); wants to have his name all around the city; want to destroy themself slowly; want to discover the truth about their benefactor; wants to be as good as their sibling, be the alpha dog.<br /> <br /> <br /> Special: they have precious object stored somewhere - but they can't directly sell them; appears to know just what you need; they are fixated on a single event of their life; they have a weirdly specific power or dark item; they're the ghoul of the most improbable person you may think of; cats follow them everywhere; they just escaped from the prison and they're on the run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T20:15:44-07:00","id":857428,"title":"","content":"I recommend seeing how they can benefit the player characters as a whole or one character specifically. My ST is known for doing a spider-web of how characters interact. For instance, if a character has a surprisingly positive relationship with his or her sire, you can see what his sire does for a 'living' and see if that's how they gather their information or something else. If their sire is surprisingly the 'Spymaster' for a power player, this is especially important that you figure out how they gather that information. Sadly, the example I am saying involves a character's sire being a male stripper. But I thought this could contribute to the conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11528-dangerus-muyoko-project","name":"Dangerus-Muyoko-Project","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T11:50:01-07:00","id":857832,"title":"","content":"&quot;Bulls eye&quot; Bill, claims he lost his foot in the &quot;sandbox&quot; when he was with the special forces, his bulging waist line and constant snacking say otherwise. Sells guns and other &quot;MIL-spec&quot; hardware out of the trunk of a car. The pieces are probably hot but the prices are cheap.<br /> <br /> Mallory Deville, this single mother works the over night shift as the head vet at the downtown animal hospital, rumor has It she can get you &quot;expired&quot; animal tranquilizers and pain pills. For a fee she can even patch people up, piss her off and she might fix you as a freebie.<br /> <br /> Dominic &quot;taggy cat&quot; Williams, this up and coming street artist will spray whatever you want on whatever you want it on for the right price. That is if you can stand him trying to add his own creative input and tumblr speak while explaining what you want done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T13:46:24-07:00","id":857897,"title":"","content":"Look at your local metro .gov sites to get an idea of exactly how extensive and sub-dividable a simple Politics group can be.<br /> <br /> Sanitation(Garbage Man-Dump Owner-Major Facility Manager, or Director of Sanitation)<br /> Construction (secretary in planning office-Large Scale City Contractor-Director of Public Works)<br /> Power (City Electrician-City Lineman-Plant Manager)<br /> Transportation (Bus Driver-City Traffic Planner-Director of Transportation)<br /> Historical Society (Volunteer Tour-Giver-Professional Archivist-Director of the Metro Area Historical Society)<br /> Prison (Clerk in Corrections Office-Prison Guard-Director of Corrections)<br /> Communications (Phone Contractor-Local Mail Office Manager-Head of Public Radio Station)<br /> <br /> Medical and Military slice up nice, too. It looks like you can expand out just about any government or heavily government-sponsored service into 5 dots. They're niche, but niche can be <i>damned </i>useful.<br /> <br /> Consider the lowly public road worker, for example. There's a King/Bachman novella/short story, I think, about an average joe who, for revenge, became a road worker, under brutal conditions, for a long time.<br /> He misappropriates some equipment to make a mid-desert highway pit trap, snugly fitted for a luxury car/limo, so he can bury it and pave it over- no chance to escape, no evidence for decades.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}